{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj5NKmAYR4ZNwKUKhz6j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you — ancient oak, iron-bound, unmarked.*\n\n*You hold up a key.*\n\n*But which key? And which lock?*\n\n*I am every door and no door. I am the concept of threshold itself. Without specificity, I remain closed — not out of malice, but out of nature.*\n\n*Name me. Name the lock. Then the key will either turn, or it won't.*\n\n*I wait, as doors do.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":106,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}